<title>UK: John Lewis UK weekly store sales up 11.1 percent.</title>
<headline>John Lewis UK weekly store sales up 11.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership said its UK department store sales rose 11.1 percent in the week to November 2 from a year earlier.</p>
<p>For the 14 weeks to November 2, department store sales were up 15.6 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Total sales, including those from the Waitrose supermarket chain, rose 10.2 percent year-on-year. For the 14-week period, sales were up 12.4 percent.</p>
<p>-- Jennifer Scott, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
